{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-131582-r4514119","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Seafood Gumbo","sourcePageId":131582,"sourceRevision":"4514119","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:43:05Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Seafood%20Gumbo&oldid=4514119","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T14:15:55.574Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Cajun recipes","Category:Louisiana recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bell pepper","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using crayfish","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using oyster","Category:Recipes using shrimp","Category:Recipes using shrimp broth and stock","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes without cooking time"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"dea4d579197d4011f2cb4bc5aa96005f8d557df0fde53b521462e1498eb96e17","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Seafood recipes\n| Servings = 10\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n==Ingredients==\n<div style=\"column-count: 2; -moz-column-count: 2\">\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Vegetable Oil|vegetable oil]]\n* ¾ cup [[Cookbook:flour|flour]]\n* 10 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] [[Cookbook:okra|okra]] (optional)\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:celery|celery]], chopped\n* 1½ cups [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]], chopped\n* 6 cloves [[Cookbook:garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n* 6 cups [[Cookbook:shrimp|shrimp]] [[Cookbook:stock|stock]] or [[Cookbook:water|water]]\n* 8 oz [[Cookbook:clam|clam]] juice (optional)\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:oregano|oregano]]\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:thyme|thyme]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaves]]\n* 1½ tsp [[Cookbook:salt|salt]]\n* ½–1 tsp [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Black pepper]] to taste\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] fresh chopped [[Cookbook:parsley|parsley]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] Andouille [[Cookbook:Sausage|sausage]], cut in pieces\n* 1 lb [[Cookbook:Shrimp|shrimp]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Pint|pint]] (or more) [[Cookbook:oyster|oysters]]\n* ½ lb [[Cookbook:crayfish|crawfish]] (optional)\n* 4 chopped [[Cookbook:Green Onion|green onions]], for topping\n</div>\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Heat oil in a 6–8 quart pot, then gradually [[Cookbook:Whisk|whisk]] in the flour. Cook over medium heat for 20 minutes until very dark reddish brown. Stir constantly, especially towards the end. The best roux is quite dark, but don’t let it burn.\n# Stir the onion, celery, bell pepper, and garlic into the roux. Cook 10 minutes (or 15 minutes if using okra).\n# Slowly and gradually whisk in the shrimp stock.\n# Add the clam juice, oregano, thyme, bay leaves, salt, cayenne, pepper, and parsley. [[Cookbook:Simmering|Simmer]] 15 minutes.\n# Add the Andouille sausage, and simmer for another 30–40 minutes.\n# Add the shrimp, oysters, and crawfish at the end, and simmer just until cooked through.\n# Top with chopped green onions.\n\n==Note, tips and variations==\n* You can add cut-up boneless chicken, or substitute chicken for the oysters, if they’re not your thing. If you don’t have Andouille sausage, smoked or Polish sausage will do fine.\n* To make shrimp stock, simmer shrimp shells in about 6½ cups of water for 20 minutes.\n* Dark roux is what makes this gumbo great.\n* Many like to serve this gumbo over rice. It also goes great with a [[Cookbook:Baguette|baguette]] or [[Cookbook:Cornbread (disambiguation)|cornbread]].\n\n[[Category:Recipes using oyster]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shrimp]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Louisiana recipes]]\n[[Category:Cajun recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using crayfish]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shrimp broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Seafood Gumbo","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"10","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"¾ cup vegetable oil","sourceText":"¾ cup vegetable oil","amountText":"¾ cup vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¾ cup flour","sourceText":"¾ cup flour","amountText":"¾ cup flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"10 oz okra (optional)","sourceText":"10 oz okra (optional)","amountText":"10 oz okra (optional)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 cups onion, chopped","sourceText":"2 cups onion, chopped","amountText":"2 cups onion, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 cup celery, chopped","sourceText":"1 cup celery, chopped","amountText":"1 cup celery, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1½ cups bell pepper, chopped","sourceText":"1½ cups bell pepper, chopped","amountText":"1½ cups bell pepper, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodB